      "title": "Drone companion controller prototype (Arduino Mega, INA219, payload release), looking for feedback",
      "link": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/drone-companion-controller-prototype-arduino-mega-ina219-payload-release-looking-for-feedback/59242",
      "summary": "Hi all, I’m Alfred, an embedded systems student at FUT Minna, Nigeria. I built this companion controller prototype during my internship at LET Innovations. It’s an Arduino Mega 2560 in C++ that does current monitoring (INA219 over I2C), ultrasonic proximity sensing with a buzzer alarm, and a servo payload release. I simulated it in Proteus and modelled the airframe in 3D. [Add here if it’s been tested on real hardware, or say it’s simulation-only so far.] Repo: GitHub - alfredoeinsteino2024/drone-companion-controller: An Arduino Mega 2560-based drone companion controller and payload release subsystem featuring real-time INA219 current telemetry, HC-SR04 proximity sensing, and automated emergency alert patterns simulated in Proteus VSM. · GitHub Feedback I’d value: a better payload-release trigger than a current threshold, converting the blocking delays to non-blocking timing, and what to test before moving from simulation to hardware. I’m now looking for a paid internship or junior firmware/embedded role (remote). If you know teams that take student contributors, I’d appreciate a pointer. 2 posts - 2 participants Read full topic",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-27T13:19:59+00:00",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-27T13:19:59+00:00",
      "source": "ROS2 Discourse",
      "section_hint": "로보틱스",
      "articleText": "Drone companion controller prototype (Arduino Mega, INA219, payload release), looking for feedback - Projects - Open Robotics Discourse Drone companion controller prototype (Arduino Mega, INA219, payload release), looking for feedback Projects embedded , arduino , microcontrollers alfredoeinsteino2024 October 27, 2026, 1:19pm 1 Hi all, I’m Alfred, an embedded systems student at FUT Minna, Nigeria. I built this companion controller prototype during my internship at LET Innovations. It’s an Arduino Mega 2560 in C++ that does current monitoring (INA219 over I2C), ultrasonic proximity sensing with a buzzer alarm, and a servo payload release. I simulated it in Proteus and modelled the airframe in 3D. [Add here if it’s been tested on real hardware, or say it’s simulation-only so far.] Repo: GitHub - alfredoeinsteino2024/drone-companion-controller: An Arduino Mega 2560-based drone companion controller and payload release subsystem featuring real-time INA219 current telemetry, HC-SR04 proximity sensing, and automated emergency alert patterns simulated in Proteus VSM. · GitHub Feedback I’d value: a better payload-release trigger than a current threshold, converting the blocking delays to non-blocking timing, and what to test before moving from simulation to hardware. I’m now looking for a paid internship or junior firmware/embedded role (remote). If you know teams that take student contributors, I’d appreciate a pointer. juliaclark October 27, 2026, 9:23pm 2 The non-blocking timing question is the one I’d tackle first, since the INA219 sampling and buzzer patterns will fight each other once you drop delay() calls; a simple millis()-based scheduler per subsystem usually covers it. For payload release, a current threshold is fragile because load varies with charge state and temperature, so consider a microswitch or optical sensor confirming the payload actually left. Before real hardware, I’d bench-test each module separately, check your I2C pull-ups and shared 5V rail under servo stall current, and verify the ultrasonic readings aren’t corrupted by motor noise. Related topics Topic Replies Views Activity micro-ROS on Arduino? :white_check_mark: Embedded embedded 24 9317 March 3, 2021 MQTT to Gazebo - Drone Simulator Projects gazebo , ros1 2 1749 April 1, 2024 Petrone Drone ROS Package Projects indigo , release , kinetic 0 1065 August 3, 2017 Drone project for personal learning Projects wg-aerial-robotics 3 417 May 21, 2025 Nectar SDK: ROS 2 companion stack for autonomous UAVs Projects ros2 , gazebo , ai , wg-aerial-robotics 0 171 August 13, 2026",
