      "title": "ROS PMC Minutes for October 20, 2026",
      "link": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/ros-pmc-minutes-for-october-20-2026/59241",
      "summary": "The ROS PMC meeting for this week was on Tuesday, October 20, 2026. The notes from the meeting are available at ROS PMC weekly meeting agenda . ROS PMC Business [@ahcorde ] Votes are going out to the PMC members for: @skye.galaxy as the ROS representative to the TGC 3 new committers @christophebedard as ROSboss for M-turtle @clalancette advised checking the voting requirements against the charter , so the process is valid. @ahcorde will check. Regular Business Buildfarm update The buildfarm builds and tests ROS packages across all supported distributions and platforms. This section covers new issues, current priorities, and infrastructure changes that affect maintainers. @skye.galaxy is reviewing the open PRs that address reentrant callback group support and data races. @mjcarroll fixed the Windows CI build failures by skipping the failing multicast tests. The nightly Clang analysis jobs will be removed after months of inactivity. @mjcarroll will open a tracking issue to record the decision. Buildfarm Issues Dashboard Waffle note-taker Waffle is a weekly meeting where maintainers triage incoming issues and pull requests that haven’t been otherwise acted upon. One person per week is",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-27T09:04:08+00:00",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-27T09:04:08+00:00",
      "source": "ROS2 Discourse",
      "section_hint": "로보틱스",
      "articleText": "ROS PMC Minutes for October 20, 2026 - Projects - Open Robotics Discourse ROS PMC Minutes for October 20, 2026 Projects meeting_notes ahcorde October 27, 2026, 9:04am 1 The ROS PMC meeting for this week was on Tuesday, October 20, 2026. The notes from the meeting are available at ROS PMC weekly meeting agenda . ROS PMC Business [@ahcorde ] Votes are going out to the PMC members for: @skye.galaxy as the ROS representative to the TGC 3 new committers @christophebedard as ROSboss for M-turtle @clalancette advised checking the voting requirements against the charter , so the process is valid. @ahcorde will check. Regular Business Buildfarm update The buildfarm builds and tests ROS packages across all supported distributions and platforms. This section covers new issues, current priorities, and infrastructure changes that affect maintainers. @skye.galaxy is reviewing the open PRs that address reentrant callback group support and data races. @mjcarroll fixed the Windows CI build failures by skipping the failing multicast tests. The nightly Clang analysis jobs will be removed after months of inactivity. @mjcarroll will open a tracking issue to record the decision. Buildfarm Issues Dashboard Waffle note-taker Waffle is a weekly meeting where maintainers triage incoming issues and pull requests that haven’t been otherwise acted upon. One person per week is assigned to be the “waffle note-taker” to both take notes in the meeting to keep the meeting as efficient as possible. Baffle maker Oct 15, 2026 - @skye.galaxy Oct 22, 2026 - Andrew Rosdistro assignments Rosdistro is a weekly assignment to monitor incoming issues and pull requests in GitHub - ros/rosdistro . Two people per week are assigned to be the rosdistro maintainers. Oct 13, 2026 - Oct 20, 2026 - @sloretz and @andrew_symington Release Management Release Management tracks the status of upcoming releases, patches, and syncs across the active ROS distributions. @christophebedard (Humble) No update. Yadunund Vijay (Rolling) No update. Marco A. Gutiérrez (Jazzy) No update. Scott Logan (Kilted) Kilted goes EOL in November 2026. @sloretz (Lyrical) The Lyrical sync is delayed 1 to 2 weeks by API breaks, so it is now expected between Oct 27 and Nov 3, 2026. @mjcarroll will complete the release scheduled for the week of Oct 20, 2026. Working Group Updates ROS Office Hours Client Library Working Group (Alberto Soragna) Last Meeting: Oct 16, 2026 Accelerated Memory Transport Working Group (@ahcorde ) Last Meeting: Oct 14, 2026 ROSGraph Working Group (@emersonknapp ) NoDL has been adopted in Polymath core. The working group has taken over maintenance of generate_parameter_library . Bazel Working Group (@andrew_symington ) The draft charter is written. Meetings will be every two weeks @andrew_symington will open a PR to the ROS documentation to register the working group. @andrew_symington , @KimMcG and @claraberendsen will hold a prep meeting to align the Bazel and Infrastructure working groups on package managers and avoid overlap. SIG Physical AI Last Meeting: Oct 16, 2026 Converged on a bimanual mobile robot as the reference application. Agenda [@mjcarroll ] AI agent guidelines and PR enforcement @mjcarroll proposed AGENTS.md files across repositories to standardize how AI agents behave. The AGENTS.md PR moves to ros2/ros2 so the skills are managed in one place Adopt AGENTS.md and AI-assisted contribution guidance (org-wide) · Issue #1887 · ros2/ros2 · GitHub . A new GitHub Action enforces the PR template and blocks submissions that don’t follow it. Please review the AGENTS.md PR and the other open PRs from @mjcarroll . [@emersonknapp ] Linting workflow @emersonknapp proposed looking at pre-commit hooks and decoupling linting from the main build, so contributors get feedback faster. @emersonknapp will post a proposal on Zulip. Action Items Everyone Vote on the TGC ROS representative, the 3 new committers and ROSboss for M-turtle. Review the AGENTS.md PR on AI interaction and development standards. Review the other open PRs from @mjcarroll . @ahcorde Send the votes for the TGC ROS representative, the 3 new committers and ROSboss for M-turtle to the PMC members. Check the voting requirements in the charter. @skye.galaxy Review the open PRs on reentrant callback group support and data races. @mjcarroll Open a tracking issue for removing the nightly Clang analysis jobs. Move the AGENTS.md PR to ros2/ros2 and fold in the recent feedback. @andrew_symington Finalize the Bazel Working Group charter and schedule meetings every two weeks. Open a PR to the ROS documentation to register the Bazel Working Group. @andrew_symington , @KimMcG , @claraberendsen and Jeff [SURNAME] Schedule a meeting to align the Bazel and Infrastructure working groups on package managers. @emersonknapp Draft a proposal for linting improvements and post it on Zulip. Related topics Topic Replies Views Activity ROS PMC Minutes for October 13, 2026 ROS PMC meeting_notes 0 69 October 20, 2026 ROS PMC Minutes for October 06, 2026 ROS PMC meeting_notes 0 52 October 20, 2026 ROS PMC Minutes for July 21, 2026 ROS PMC ros , minutes , pmc 0 100 July 27, 2026 ROS PMC Minutes for March 17, 2026 ROS PMC 0 148 March 17, 2026 ROS PMC Minutes for August 18th, 2026 ROS PMC 0 136 August 25, 2026",
      "articleUrl": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/ros-pmc-minutes-for-october-20-2026/59241",
