      "title": "New course: Agentic Robotics with ROS 2, from AI agents to VLA models (code on GitHub)",
      "link": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/new-course-agentic-robotics-with-ros-2-from-ai-agents-to-vla-models-code-on-github/59239",
      "summary": "Hello everyone, I have published a self-paced course that connects ROS 2 with today’s AI methods. Everything runs on one simulated greenhouse robot, with one task: inspect the tomato rows. What you build ROS 2 basics: nodes, topics, services and actions ROS 2 skill servers that an AI agent (LLM) calls as tools A dataset of 49 human demonstrations (4,228 frames) A SmolVLA model trained on that data, used as the robot’s “pick” skill An honest test of the model, with simple baselines to compare against What you need: Ubuntu 24.04 and Python. Modules 0 to 2 run on 8 GB of RAM with no GPU. Training the VLA model needs an NVIDIA GPU with 4 GB of memory. Code: the full workspace (robot, skill servers, agent scripts, demos) is on GitHub and linked in module 0. Course: Agentic Robotics: From LLM Tool-Calling to Vision-Language-Action Models Feedback on the design is very welcome. 1 post - 1 participant Read full topic",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-27T08:30:34+00:00",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-27T08:30:34+00:00",
      "source": "ROS2 Discourse",
      "section_hint": "로보틱스",
      "articleText": "New course: Agentic Robotics with ROS 2, from AI agents to VLA models (code on GitHub) - Training & Education - Open Robotics Discourse New course: Agentic Robotics with ROS 2, from AI agents to VLA models (code on GitHub) Training & Education ros2 , gazebo , ai , deep-learning Anis_Koubaa October 27, 2026, 8:30am 1 Hello everyone, I have published a self-paced course that connects ROS 2 with today’s AI methods. Everything runs on one simulated greenhouse robot, with one task: inspect the tomato rows. What you build ROS 2 basics: nodes, topics, services and actions ROS 2 skill servers that an AI agent (LLM) calls as tools A dataset of 49 human demonstrations (4,228 frames) A SmolVLA model trained on that data, used as the robot’s “pick” skill An honest test of the model, with simple baselines to compare against What you need: Ubuntu 24.04 and Python. Modules 0 to 2 run on 8 GB of RAM with no GPU. Training the VLA model needs an NVIDIA GPU with 4 GB of memory. Code: the full workspace (robot, skill servers, agent scripts, demos) is on GitHub and linked in module 0. Course: Agentic Robotics: From LLM Tool-Calling to Vision-Language-Action Models 06_ros2_llm_integration 1672×879 297 KB Feedback on the design is very welcome. Related topics Topic Replies Views Activity AgenticROS: Connects ROS with OpenClaw, Claude (code, desktop, dispatch), and Google Gemini Projects ros2 , ai 18 1499 October 16, 2026 Senior Robotics Engineer ROS 2, Hardware and AI Jobs ros2 0 377 May 28, 2025 📢 Announcing CRISP: Closing the Gap Between ROS 2 and Robot Learning ROS General release , ros2 , deep-learning , ros2_control , pixi 0 801 August 18, 2025 Announcing new ROS upskilling program — Mastering Robotics & AI using ROS 2 and NVIDIA Isaac! 🤖 Training & Education ros2 , gazebo , course , nvidia 0 253 October 23, 2025 Vision Language Models for Robotics | ROS Developers Open Class #179 Training & Education ros , ai 0 2817 December 15, 2023",
