      "title": "ROS2 Driver for Blueprint Subsea Oculus M3000d",
      "link": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/ros2-driver-for-blueprint-subsea-oculus-m3000d/59261",
      "summary": "Hi everyone! I recently open-sourced the ROS2 driver that I’m using for my M3000d. You can find it here: Repository AlePuglisi/oculus-m3000d-ros2-cpp-driver GitHub - AlePuglisi/oculus-m3000d-ros2-cpp-driver: Driver for the Blueprint Subsea Oculus M3000d... Driver for the Blueprint Subsea Oculus M3000d Imaging Sonar. ROS2 Jazzy interface and Low Level C++ Sensor Driver. I worked on this last year by extending ENSTA Bretagne’s oculus_ros2, which didn’t include support for the M3000d. I have been busy with other tasks, and I recently started maintaining it again and fixing some bugs. I saw that the most-supported driver for the Oculus sonar, liboculus , has a discussion about the M3000d and should support this sonar. I haven’t tested it, to be honest. This driver is specifically updated for the M3000d, as I didn’t notice before that the libocolus driver fully supported the M3000d… The only problem I’m currently encountering is the pingRate reconfiguration, which is clamped to 9 Hz even if I request 15 or 40 Hz… I haven’t investigated it yet extensively. Let me know if it is useful for the community! I’m also working on a lightweight, easy-to-modify C++ interface that substitutes the p",
